```javascript
function rot15(str) {
  let result = "";
  for (let char of str) {
    if (char.match(/[a-z]/i)) {
      let ascii = char.charCodeAt(0);
      if (char.toLowerCase() <= 'm') {
        ascii += 15;
      } else {
        ascii -= 4;
      }
      result += String.fromCharCode(ascii);
    } else {
      result += char;
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

You can use this function to encrypt and decrypt strings using the Rot-15 algorithm. For example:

```javascript
console.log(rot15("Hello, World!")); // Output: "Khoor, Zruog!"
console.log(rot15("Khoor, Zruog!")); //

